    <edge source="entity-134991ef70c5cbd0c69f002556d0" target="entity-51e5a7e7be1f9a89d48f72d8f70c" id="candidate-d9e143396b3cf5761ec09494d6568bdc">
      <data key="d2">candidate-d9e143396b3cf5761ec09494d6568bdc</data>
      <data key="d3">is_linked_to</data>
      <data key="d4">local_connection_supported</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">0</data>
      <data key="d7">The development of crop root systems is intricately linked to the soil's structural looseness or compactness.</data>
      <data key="d8">associative</data>
      <data key="d9">{"crop_or_species": "", "population": "", "condition": "", "comparator": "", "metric": ""}</data>
      <data key="d10">False</data>
      <data key="d11">Exploring the link between soil health and crop productivity</data>
      <data key="d12">The development of crop root systems is intricately linked to the soil’s structural looseness or compactness, with soil microorganisms playing a crucial regulatory role in root system growth (Sharma et al., 2021).</data>
      <data key="d13">["neighbor-7c5cc886733b793bf5872c5cbb83", "neighbor-aca20020718e0390749f2f989b1f"]</data>
      <data key="d14">False</data>
      <data key="d15">True</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="entity-3415427df404937e606a0ad77914" target="entity-4a93ec3a99fc98b135386253c701" id="candidate-790650449a136ea64ca703b30ff4cb7b">
      <data key="d2">candidate-790650449a136ea64ca703b30ff4cb7b</data>
      <data key="d3">contributes_to</data>
      <data key="d4">local_connection_supported</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">0</data>
      <data key="d7">The soil microbial community contributes to crop growth and development through the facilitation of nutrient cycling.</data>
      <data key="d8">causal</data>
      <data key="d9">{"crop_or_species": "", "population": "", "condition": "through the facilitation of nutrient cycling", "comparator": "", "metric": ""}</data>
      <data key="d10">False</data>
      <data key="d11">Exploring the link between soil health and crop productivity</data>
      <data key="d12">The soil microbial community contributes to crop growth and development through the decomposition of organic matter, nitrogen fixation, and the facilitation of nutrient cycling (Yadav et al., 2021).</data>
      <data key="d13">["neighbor-ecb4766ab62cfe3aa03519c91846"]</data>
      <data key="d14">False</data>
      <data key="d15">True</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="entity-3415427df404937e606a0ad77914" target="entity-b31c464f97682a4e095413766934" id="candidate-9edb61e734efb2bb83853dc19b8aa5b5">
      <data key="d2">candidate-9edb61e734efb2bb83853dc19b8aa5b5</data>
      <data key="d3">suppresses</data>
      <data key="d4">local_connection_supported</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">0</data>
      <data key="d7">A rich and diverse soil microbial community can suppress soil-borne diseases.</data>
      <data key="d8">descriptive</data>
      <data key="d9">{"crop_or_species": "", "population": "", "condition": "", "comparator": "", "metric": ""}</data>
      <data key="d10">False</data>
      <data key="d11">Exploring the link between soil health and crop productivity</data>
      <data key="d12">A rich and diverse microbial community can enhance nutrient cycling efficiency, suppress soil-borne diseases, and promote plant growth and development (Niu et al., 2020).</data>
      <data key="d13">["neighbor-fc4cc7ff9c8d9487d7e049073343", "neighbor-675c55ed7c063ecd3cf3323de5e1"]</data>
      <data key="d14">False</data>
      <data key="d15">True</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="entity-3415427df404937e606a0ad77914" target="entity-34bf8e01e036736e4af16f19e223" id="candidate-4b569c4dfe45423e774249cdabe1753a">
      <data key="d2">candidate-4b569c4dfe45423e774249cdabe1753a</data>
      <data key="d3">produce</data>
      <data key="d4">local_connection_supported</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">0</data>
      <data key="d7">Rhizosphere microorganisms produce auxins that promote plant growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d8">descriptive</data>
      <data key="d9">{"crop_or_species": "", "population": "", "condition": "", "comparator": "", "metric": ""}</data>
      <data key="d10">False</data>
      <data key="d11">Exploring the link between soil health and crop productivity</data>
      <data key="d12">Additionally, rhizosphere nitrogen-fixing bacteria can form symbiotic nodules with plants, converting nitrogen gas into nitrogen compounds that are absorbable by plants, thus providing essential nutrients for plant growth (Fahde et al., 2023 Furthermore, rhizosphere microorganisms can produce auxins, which Table 2 Microorganisms release organic acids and enzymes that promote the breakdown of organic matter, thereby improving the utilization of crop nutrients. Microorganism Released organic acids Released enzymes type Bacteria Acetic acid, Citric acid Cellulases, Proteases Fungi Oxalic acid, Gluconic Ligninases, Amylases acid Actinomycetes Lactic acid, Propionic Chitinases, Phosphatases acid Archaea Sulfuric acid Ammonia Oxidases Protozoa Acetic acid, Butyric Various Hydrolytic acidEnzymes Yeasts Malic Acid, Succinic Invertases, Lipases acid Ecotoxicology and Environmental Safety 289 (2025) 117703 promote plant growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d13">["neighbor-78d0dd640de7d4bb9c29fca1d4f2", "neighbor-a5fd95f3a7ccfaeb75a174abe93f"]</data>
      <data key="d14">False</data>
      <data key="d15">True</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="entity-3415427df404937e606a0ad77914" target="entity-9c617d6f11b032444076f0e2a3b2" id="candidate-a60d5f0b43cf964fecee3cb142c5466b">
      <data key="d2">candidate-a60d5f0b43cf964fecee3cb142c5466b</data>
      <data key="d3">decomposes_to</data>
      <data key="d4">local_connection_supported</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">0</data>
      <data key="d7">Microorganisms decompose insoluble phosphates into forms that plants can readily absorb.</data>
      <data key="d8">descriptive</data>
      <data key="d9">{"crop_or_species": "", "population": "", "condition": "", "comparator": "", "metric": ""}</data>
      <data key="d10">False</data>
      <data key="d11">Exploring the link between soil health and crop productivity</data>
      <data key="d12">Microorganisms are also capable of decomposing insoluble phosphates, converting them into forms that plants can readily absorb.</data>
      <data key="d13">["neighbor-6487956fa7a262a29bf39bdf55d2", "neighbor-617282b509440aa70484c9782329"]</data>
      <data key="d14">False</data>
      <data key="d15">True</data>
